# Redesigned 2026-08-31 (owner spec): a path PORTION that REACHES a filesystem
# sink is the finding. A literal nothing opens does not count; a bare filename
# is allowed; anything computed is clean.
#
# NARROWED 2026-09-01 (owner ruling): only an ABSOLUTE ROOT -- a drive letter or
# a UNC lead -- is a finding. A hardcoded RELATIVE portion is allowed, so the
# LoadFromFile line moved from the positives to the negatives. It is kept as a
# live negative rather than deleted: firing on it is the exact regression this
# narrowing removes, and a deleted line asserts nothing.
#
# LINE NUMBERS MOVED with it -- the fixture gained a two-line comment, so the
# old 18/21/24/26 are now 20/23/26/28. These are absolute line numbers; re-derive
# them from the .pas whenever it is edited.
#
# The negatives are load-bearing: with only the one positive this file would
# pass against the OLD unscoped rule, which fired on every drive-letter literal.
hardcoded-absolute-path 16
!hardcoded-absolute-path 20
!hardcoded-absolute-path 23
!hardcoded-absolute-path 26
!hardcoded-absolute-path 28
